package api

import (
	"fmt"
	"net/http"

	"github.com/sjawhar/envoy/internal/dispatch/model"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodPost,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/going/runs/{id}/undo",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: fmt.Sprintf("Undo the caller's own command-bar run, as the credential that sends this and in-process: every call of the run that landed a request (each row of its plan that ran), newest first, each by the undo its tool states. write_back reads the item's value now and writes back the value the call found, field by field, only where the value now is the one the call left (an issue's fields and rank, an ask's text, a comment's or an issue message's body, a document's content as a further version); a later value another writer left is kept, its field refused 409 %s naming what it holds and who changed that field after the call landed - read from what came after the call's landing, never from the item's newest event, and named as another writer where no event after the landing names one - and the rest is written back. A post's body is written back through its PATCH route, which answered the body the edit replaced as previous; a post its author deleted after the run is kept, named deleted and by whom, with no part of its body, and the route's 409 %s, %s or %s is kept as another writer's change. reverse runs the call's reverse: a claim released - none where the claim route answered claim_changed false - a release taken back only where the holder it released is the one the undo's own claim is recorded as, the session the caller's credential proved or else the person (409 %s otherwise, with nothing written), a follow unfollowed, a resolved comment reopened, an opened ask or approval request retracted - none where the approval route answered opened false - and a suggestion of the run rejected while it is still open. close_created closes the issue the call created, posting nothing on it, only while its status is the one the create left it in - none for a create its route answered 200 with the issue Dispatch already held for the external reference it named. not_undone names the call sent, not undone: a message, a broadcast, a review; a delete of a comment or an issue message %q, since nothing restores a deleted post; and a record of a deploy %q, since no route removes one. What a call found and left is read off what its route answered of its own transaction, recorded beside its landing, never off a read since, so a run whose process ended after a write landed is undone all the same; a call whose record does not say what it left is refused 409 %s, one whose route found a value the read its row was approved over did not see 409 %s, a call that names no write tool 409 %s, and one whose tool states an undo this server has no way to run 501 %s, each with nothing undone. Every undo that puts a value back has the route it writes through decide, under that write's own lock, that the item still holds what the call left, by an in-process condition the undo carries on the request's context, never a body member, so a change another writer makes between the undo's read and its write is kept. An undo sends one request at the most, which records its landing in its route's own transaction under the key of the call it undoes, with the line this answers, so a second undo of the run, after a crash or beside the first, answers each call whose undo landed from that landing and sends nothing twice. Whether an undo landed is read from that landing, not from its route's status: a request its route answered below 300 that committed nothing - the item already stood as the undo asked, as a follow of a session that follows the ask already answers 204 - is answered ok, saying it changed nothing and there is nothing to undo; that answer, and a call kept whole because another writer changed it since the run (409 %s, found by the undo's read with nothing sent, or by its route's refusal), is recorded as the call's undo landing in a statement of its own, so a later undo answers it from there and sends nothing again. A press under an Idempotency-Key binds the run as its key's recovery point before it sends anything, so a repeat under the key, however the first press ended - its process gone mid-walk included - walks the run again and answers its lines, Idempotency-Replayed: ?1, rather than 409 KEY_COMMITTED. Answers 200 {lines: [{plan, row, tool, item, undo, outcome, fields: [{field, ok, message, now?, by?}]}]}, one line per landed call, fields one per field of the item the call changed, a field's message never naming its own field; a field kept because another writer changed it after the run also carries now, the value it holds as the item's read answers it, and by {kind, id}, who changed it after the call landed, absent where no event after the landing names one. 404 %s for a run that is not the caller's, that the store does not hold, or whose conversation History no longer lists: its newest run is older than seven days.", codeGoingUndoChanged, codeCommentChanged, codeMessageChanged, codePostDeleted, codeGoingUndoNotCallers, goingDeletedNotUndone, goingRecordedNotUndone, codeGoingUndoAfterUnread, codeGoingUndoBeforeUnread, codeGoingUndoUnknown, codeGoingUndoUnserved, codeGoingUndoChanged, codeGoingRunNotFound),
	Handler:     (*server).undoGoingRun,
	WriteClass:  scopeSession,
	ID:          &idRoute{Reason: "a going run's id, which the route undoes for its own author alone and answers for itself"},
	OAuthScopes: routeScopeSet{model.ScopePerson},
	Shape:       routeShape{Status: http.StatusOK, Response: goingUndoAnswer{}},
})
